<h1>Chase to Hyatt Transfer: Ratio, Value &amp; Calculator</h1>
<p class="sub">Calculate exact World of Hyatt® points received from Chase Ultimate Rewards® points. Includes 2026 card-tier ratios (1:1 vs. 4:3), 1,000-point increments, cash-rate CPP examples, and when not to transfer.</p>

<div class="direct-answer">
  <strong>Direct Answer:</strong> Chase Ultimate Rewards® transfers to World of Hyatt® in <strong>increments of 1,000 points</strong> (minimum 1,000 points) with <strong>$0 transfer fee</strong>. As of October 2026, the ratio depends on your eligible card: <strong>1:1</strong> (1,000 Chase points = 1,000 Hyatt points) on <strong>Chase Sapphire Reserve®</strong> and <strong>Sapphire Reserve for Business℠</strong>, or <strong>4:3</strong> (1,000 Chase points = 750 Hyatt points) on <strong>Chase Sapphire Preferred®</strong> and <strong>Ink Business Preferred®</strong>. Transfers are typically instant (official terms allow up to 7 business days) and are strictly one-way and irreversible.
</div>

